vLLM exposes a fully OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings endpoint (for embedding models like intfloat/e5-mistral-7b-instruct, BAAI/bge-* etc.). Sister engines Langertha::Engine::LlamaCpp, Langertha::Engine::OllamaOpenAI, Langertha::Engine::LMStudioOpenAI all compose Langertha::Role::Embedding and advertise the capability. Langertha::Engine::vLLM does not — composing the Embedding role + adding createEmbedding to _build_supported_operations + default_embedding_model would close the gap and match what vLLM serves today. Reference: https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/serving/online_serving/ confirms /v1/embeddings is in the OpenAI-compatible surface.
vLLM composes Embedding role, createEmbedding in _build_supported_operations, default_embedding_model = 'default'. New t/65b_vllm_embeddings.t (11 offline tests) pins POST /v1/embeddings body shape. t/10 + t/65 extended. Bundled with #71/72/73/74.
